# Docs demo icons = Phosphor

Live demos and MDX code fences that need **content** icons (addon, `icon`, empty-state glyph, …) import from `@phosphor-icons/react`. Do **not** use `@viraui/icons` / `@viraui/icons/react` in those examples.

## Why

Docs teach that slots take any `ReactNode`. Phosphor is already a site dependency and matches the consumer “bring your own icons” story. `@viraui/icons` stays for **site chrome** only (nav via `viraIconsPlugin`, shared `<Icon name="…" />`).

## Do

```tsx
import { Download, FloppyDisk, Trash } from '@phosphor-icons/react';

<Button addon={<Download />}>Download</Button>
```

## Do not

```tsx
import { Download } from '@viraui/icons/react';
```

## Out of scope

- Nav / frontmatter `icon:` strings resolved by `viraIconsPlugin`
- Foundation `/foundation/icons` page may still show Lucide + Phosphor + sprite side-by-side to prove “any library”
- Built-in chrome inside `@viraui/react` (chevrons, checks, close) — not content glyphs
